<title>Suggested Approach to Evaluation of the Infant with Suspected Hirschsprung's Disease.</title>
<graphic href="eee0557-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Hirschsprung's disease suspected: constipation, abdominal distension, delayed passage of meconium, tight anal canal. Age?</label>
<path target="cell-2">Younger than 3 years</path>
<path target="cell-3">3 years or older</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Suction rectal biopsy</label>
<path target="cell-4">No ganglia</path>
<path target="cell-5">Ganglia present</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-4">
<label>Full thickness biopsy</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>Treat constipation</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Barium enema and&#x002F;or rectal manometry</label>
<path target="cell-4">Abnormal</path>
<path target="cell-5">Normal result</path>
</cell>
</algorithm>
